      "writtenOn": "2019-11-20T16:51:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand \"I think this should be off because it prevents non-auto drp toggle\".\n\nThis \"/* DRP Toggle */ set_state_tc(port, TC_UNATTACHED_SRC);\" is the non-auto drp toggle, which we should be doing when \"drp_state[port] \u003d\u003d PD_DRP_TOGGLE_ON\", not when \"drp_state[port] \u003d\u003d PD_DRP_TOGGLE_OFF\".\n\nNow I\u0027m looking at this again, there is also a problem with swapping the other way in tc_unattached_src_run() on line 2210 not checking drp_state policy at all.\n\nCompare to the old TCPMv1 implementation: usb_pd_protocol.c lines 3332 and 3955.",
      "parentUuid": "d84912fc_aad6cda6",
      "revId": "8a80b7f7dda33063ac3fcdcb689018c9976911cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
