    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6286b10e_bf8df773",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1736,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-20T19:31:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PD_DRP_TOGGLE_ON/PD_DRP_TOGGLE_OFF controls whether auto toggling is on or off not drp toggleing in general. The base CL does not use this FLAG. It was only added to prevent drp toggling when auto toggle is enabled. Perhaps the name of the flags should be changed to PD_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE_ON and PD_DRP_AUTO_TOGGLE_OFF.",
      "parentUuid": "313a1114_7473bbe9",
      "revId": "8a80b7f7dda33063ac3fcdcb689018c9976911cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dbbd78c7_158c75cf",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1736,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-11-20T19:49:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I disagree: the drp_state policy applies equally to auto or non-auto toggling, see the comments documenting enum pd_dual_role_states. TCPMv2 should match TCPMv1 behavior. Support for this policy needs to be added to TCPMv2 for both auto and non-auto toggling.\n\n\u003e It was only added to prevent drp toggling when auto toggle is enabled.\n\nThat\u0027s a different flag PD_FLAGS_TCPC_DRP_TOGGLE in TCPMv1. In TCPMv2 I don\u0027t think you\u0027ll need the same flag, because things are better organized into different states.\n\nAdding support for drp_state policy could be moved out of this CL into its own if you want to unblock this one.",
      "parentUuid": "6286b10e_bf8df773",
      "revId": "8a80b7f7dda33063ac3fcdcb689018c9976911cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
